# Coverage Gate (CI, Not Routine Local)

CI enforces ≥85% line coverage via `scripts/run-coverage.sh`. That job is slow (instrumented
rebuild + full suite + gcov). Do **not** run it on every feature change or before every push.

## Default local verify

For normal work, prefer:

1. Desired-behavior tests for the change
2. `ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure` (or the focused gtest filter)

Do **not** routinely run `scripts/run-coverage.sh`.

## When to run coverage locally

Run `scripts/run-coverage.sh` only when:

- The CI **coverage** job failed, or
- The user explicitly asks for a coverage run / to clear the coverage floor

Then add focused tests that exercise **missed lines in the new/changed code**. Do not pad
unrelated modules just to raise the percentage. Update `docs/testing.md` / README coverage notes
when the reported percentage changes.

## Anti-pattern

```text
BAD:  Run full coverage after every small src/ edit (wastes minutes for little signal)
GOOD: Ship with ctest + desired-behavior tests; fix coverage when CI reports a miss
```
